THE MODULE UNDER REVIEW: scripts/build_adjudication_packet_2026_08_19.py

--- THE FILE, IN FULL ---
"""BLIND ADJUDICATION PACKET for the 130 trials the mechanical screener could not settle.

TWO INDEPENDENT INSTRUMENTS, ASKED THE SAME QUESTION, NEITHER TOLD WHAT THE OTHER OR I THINK.

    They are asked to CLASSIFY THE ARMS, not to confirm a verdict. A reviewer handed a verdict
    and asked whether it is right agrees far more often than one handed the raw material and
    asked what it shows -- and the whole value of a second family is that it did not inherit
    the first one's reading.

The packet therefore contains ONLY the registry arm structures. It does not contain: the
screener's verdict, the disposition vocabulary, the review's criteria, the word "excluded", or
any hint that these 130 are the residue of anything. A reader of the packet cannot tell which
answer would be convenient.

FAMILIES, and why three rather than two: Claude (anthropic) wrote the screener, so Claude is
the instrument under test and cannot also be its own check. Codex (openai) and agy (Gemini,
google) are the two independent readings. Where they AGREE the answer is taken and spot-checked
against a coded field; where they DIFFER the case is read by hand. That is the method that
found the arm-role defect and it is the only one here that has ever caught a
withholding-direction error.

EVIDENCE IS INLINE. agy has no file tools in this configuration, so a packet that names a path
is a packet it cannot read -- and a model that cannot read its evidence will answer anyway.
"""
import io
import json
import os
import sys

REPO = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(REPO, "ssot"))
os.environ.setdefault(
    "RM_CTGOV_CACHE",
    "F:/claude-temp/claude/F--rapidmeta-ssot-shell/"
    "eb4d84e5-8a24-4c3b-afe2-34bd91c20bc7/scratchpad/.ctgov-raw-cache")

import ctgov_transport as X          # noqa: E402

SCREEN = os.path.join(REPO, "evidence", "2026-08-19-batch1", "ablation_medical_screening.json")
OUT_DIR = ("F:/claude-temp/claude/F--rapidmeta-ssot-shell/"
           "6b629e1e-cc8c-4565-af03-e40341ee43f3/scratchpad")

TASK = """You are reading registered clinical trial arm structures from ClinicalTrials.gov.

For EACH trial below, decide two things FROM THE ARM DATA SHOWN AND NOTHING ELSE:

  A) Does any arm deliver CATHETER-BASED ABLATION OF ATRIAL FIBRILLATION as that arm's
     treatment? This means pulmonary vein isolation, radiofrequency, cryoballoon, pulsed-field
     or laser ablation of atrial tissue.
     IMPORTANT: ablation of the AV node / AV junction / His bundle is NOT this -- that ablates
     the conduction system and requires a pacemaker. Surgical or thoracoscopic maze performed
     during cardiac surgery is NOT this either.
     Answer: YES / NO / UNCLEAR

  B) Does any OTHER arm serve as a control that is NOT itself an atrial ablation -- that is,
     drug therapy of any kind, usual/standard/conventional care, or no treatment?
     Answer: YES / NO / UNCLEAR

Output EXACTLY one line per trial, no commentary, in this format:
NCTxxxxxxxx | A=YES|NO|UNCLEAR | B=YES|NO|UNCLEAR

Use UNCLEAR whenever the arm names genuinely do not tell you. UNCLEAR is a correct and
expected answer; do not guess to avoid it.
"""


def main():
    sys.stdout = io.TextIOWrapper(sys.stdout.buffer, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    rows = json.load(io.open(SCREEN, encoding="utf-8"))["trials"]
    todo = [r["nct"] for r in rows if r["verdict"] == "NEEDS_ADJUDICATION"]
    print("trials to adjudicate: %d" % len(todo))

    blocks = []
    for nct in todo:
        st, study, det = X.fetch_raw(nct, fields="protocolSection,hasResults")
        if st != X.OK:
            continue
        p = X.require_raw_v2(study, nct)["protocolSection"]
        arms = (p.get("armsInterventionsModule") or {}).get("armGroups") or []
        lines = ["%s" % nct]
        for a in arms:
            names = "; ".join(str(n) for n in (a.get("interventionNames") or [])) or "(none)"
            lines.append("    [%s] %s -- %s"
                         % (a.get("type") or "?", a.get("label") or "?", names))
        blocks.append("\n".join(lines))

    os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)
    # Chunked so no single prompt is so long that a model starts summarising instead of
    # answering. Same chunks to both seats, so a disagreement is never an artefact of
    # different batching.
    CHUNK = 33
    paths = []
    for i in range(0, len(blocks), CHUNK):
        part = blocks[i:i + CHUNK]
        text = TASK + "\n" + ("\n\n".join(part)) + "\n"
        path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, "adjudication_packet_%02d.txt" % (i // CHUNK + 1))
        with io.open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(text)
        paths.append(path)
        print("   wrote %s  (%d trials, %d chars)" % (path, len(part), len(text)))

    with io.open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, "adjudication_ids.json"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(json.dumps(todo, indent=1))
    print("\nSAME CHUNKS TO BOTH SEATS. A disagreement must be about the trial, never about "
          "how the\nquestion was cut up.")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())

